    "body": "The final microbatch’s DP-outer reduction currently shares the inner reduce-scatter stream. The next parameter group waits on that stream before packing its gradients, so a long outer reduction can stall backward computation.\n\nThis PR moves the deferred DP-outer reduction to a dedicated outer_reduce_scatter_stream owned by the FSDP context:\n\nWait for the producing inner reduction before launching outer communication.\nAllow subsequent gradient packing and inner reductions to proceed while outer communication runs.\nJoin both reduction streams in finish_grad_sync() before consuming the finalized gradients.\nEstablish the outer-stream dependency at backward entry for CUDA Graph capture.\nKeep fused expert-gradient scaling on the stream that finalizes the gradients.\nThe change preserves the existing reduce_partial_gradients() API, persistent gradient buffers, and all-gather path.\n\nValidation\n\n- Full MFSDP v2 unit suite passed, including CUDA Graph and stream-synchronization coverage.\n- The combined optimization stack completed 20 DSv4 Flash HSDP iterations on 128 GB200 GPUs with full-iteration and optimizer CUDA Graphs, with no skipped or NaN iterations.\n- Related to #6973, which addresses the same overlap opportunity. This implementation keeps the existing gradient-reduction API and performs the stream switch inside the final-microbatch branch.\n",
    "changed_files": 3,
